---
description: Ban owned NamedTuple/namedtuple and positional tuple value objects
globs: "**/*.py"
alwaysApply: true
---

# No owned positional tuple value objects

Do not invent domain shapes as positional tuples, `collections.namedtuple`, or
`typing.NamedTuple`. Prefer a frozen `@dataclass` (one type per file).

## Forbidden

```python
Point = namedtuple("Point", ["x", "y"])
class Rect(NamedTuple):
    x: int
    y: int
    w: int
    h: int
def bounds(...) -> tuple[int, int, int, int]: ...
```

## Allowed

```python
@dataclass(frozen=True)
class FrameRect:
    x: int
    y: int
    width: int
    height: int
```

Heterogeneous multi-value returns also belong in a dataclass — see `python-no-object-typing`
and `solid-python` (Flask `Response | tuple[Response, int]` remains the sole status-pair exception).
